# Documentation updates

When you **add or change a public editor feature** (props, commands, chrome, serialisation, or host APIs), update both documentation surfaces before finishing:

1. **[`README.md`](README.md)** — usage contract for consumers. Add or revise the prop row, section, and TSX example.
2. **Playground documentation** — the Documentation view renders `README.md`, so README changes show there. Also update playground demos when the feature is interactive:
   - sidebar controls in [`playground/src/App.tsx`](playground/src/App.tsx)
   - popup snippets in [`playground/src/codeExamples.ts`](playground/src/codeExamples.ts)
   - playground copy in [`playground/src/i18n/messages.ts`](playground/src/i18n/messages.ts) (`en` and `es`)

Do not ship a public API change with only code. If a playground control exists for the feature, its Code examples popup must match the README snippet.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — new Editor prop, README and playground examples left unchanged
<Editor transformHtml={sanitize} />

// ✅ GOOD — README section + playground snippet (and a sidebar demo if it is togglable)
```
